{
  "$note": [
    "Written by hand (least upper bound and type-parameter binding, with worked cases); never generated. Read by C# only (TypeParameterBindingContractTests, TypeParameterBindingMutationTests).",
    "`vocabulary` adds host types to the library's: an atom names a CLR stand-in of the test (`clr`), its rows (`widensTo`) and claims; a constructor its allowed arguments.",
    "`literalTerms`: a literal as JSON and its term, null when it has none.",
    "`evidence`: what a site gives for the parameters of its declared term, from a closed `source` term (`null` is the null literal) or a `literal`. `T >= X` is lower-bound evidence, `T = X` exact evidence.",
    "`resolution`: one parameter's evidence and constraints, and what the binding pass answers: a `term`, `unbound`, or a `refusal` rule id.",
    "`lub`: the least upper bound table; null is undefined.",
    "`cases`: worked graphs. `blocks` declares the shapes they use: `typeParameters`, `inputs` and `outputs` as name to declared term, `required` inputs, `subCanvases` with their own `inputs` and `outputs`, Enum `configuration` fields; IterateOver and Filter shaped as the library's blocks of those names. A canvas lists `nodes` (`id`, `block`, optional `config`, `typeArguments` and `subCanvases`), `wires` from `node.output` to `node.input` (a bare `node` to `node` orders two nodes and maps nothing), and `literals` on `node.input`. Every canvas gets a WorkflowInput node (`start` at the root, `entry` in a body) wired to every node nothing else feeds, and a literal is a mapping on that node's wire. `expect.refusals` is the whole list of rule, canvas, node and port (null where the diagnostic names none), in any order; `expect.ports` maps `<canvas>:<node>.<in|out>.<port>` to its effective term, or to `unbound`; the root canvas is empty and a body is `<node>/<branch>`."
  ],
